  PLAYER swipe indicator, active page - the literal Figma vector.

    instance 2402:31398 -> component master 2401:38 "Shape=9-sided cookie"
    vector 2401:39, master viewport 380x380, child at (27.9998, 29.8999)
    54-segment vector network

  The nine-lobed cookie, copied verbatim from the component master rather than
  derived. It replaces a cosine-lobed disc whose amplitude had been solved from
  the recorded 8.53 x 8.42 bounding box - a good fit, and still a reconstruction.
  The two agree on that box: 324.0002 x 319.9503 of a 380 viewport drawn at 10dp
  is 8.53 x 8.42, which is exactly what the snapshot records.

  The drawable is the 10dp slot, not the ink: the group transform is the
  component master's, so the marker lands where the component puts it and the
  ImageView's 10dp slot needs no centring arithmetic.

  One segment of the supplied path is removed here. It is an export artefact, not
  a design change, and the evidence is in the path itself.

  Flattening a vector network into one contour emits degenerate segments - curves
  that return to their own start point. This path has 18 of them, and seventeen
  form a perfectly regular pattern: nine straying 1.178 units from their anchor
  and nine straying 0.558, one of each per lobe, all far under a pixel at the
  26px this renders at. The eighteenth, at (126.932, 10.388), strays **26.13
  units - 22 times the next largest** - because its control points landed at
  y=-3.46, outside the shape. It paints a thin spur up and to the left of the top
  lobe: 3 pixels at render size, and the only feature on the whole outline that
  breaks the component's nine-fold symmetry. `Shape=9-sided cookie` has nine
  identical lobes; a spur on one of them is not part of it.

  So that one segment is dropped and the other 53 are untouched - no
  simplification, no redrawing, every remaining pathData number verbatim.

  A second artefact of the same mis-flattened seam is NOT repaired, because
  repairing it would mean redrawing geometry: the top lobe comes out flat rather
  than rounded, which is why the path measures 315.76 x 312.52 against the
  324.000244 x 319.950256 that both the manifest's childNodeSize and the
  canonical snapshot record for this node. That is 0.22 slot units, and the lobes
  themselves are only about 0.6px deep at 10dp - so it is a sub-pixel difference
  on screen. Fixing it properly means re-exporting the node, not editing this
  file.

  Otherwise only the fill is changed, to the repo's #FFFFFF placeholder: the
  colour is `primary`, applied through player_swipe_tint.
-->
